{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>'Ash.</b> They are seven stars: Kesil and Kimah. Two great stars, one on the left side of the inclined sphere and the second on the south side, and 'Ash is on the north side of the great sphere." "<b>And the chambers of Teman.</b> These are the stars that are on the south side of the great sphere, and because the inhabited world is on the left side and those stars are not seen, therefore he called them \"chambers,\" as though they are in a hidden place."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:11.616175243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}